WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.319
2035 came early

00:00:02.838 --> 00:00:03.793
A new essay

00:00:03.605 --> 00:00:04.689
argues the future

00:00:04.501 --> 00:00:06.611
once expected by 2035

00:00:06.423 --> 00:00:07.684
has already arrived

00:00:07.885 --> 00:00:08.651
years ahead of

00:00:08.463 --> 00:00:09.217
schedule

00:00:09.742 --> 00:00:10.602
It looks back

00:00:10.426 --> 00:00:12.135
from 2035 at how

00:00:11.947 --> 00:00:13.208
JavaScript became the

00:00:13.020 --> 00:00:14.164
default language for

00:00:13.976 --> 00:00:14.895
all software

00:00:14.978 --> 00:00:16.086
a story told

00:00:15.921 --> 00:00:17.194
in a 2009

00:00:17.006 --> 00:00:17.914
talk by Jeff

00:00:17.726 --> 00:00:18.338
Atwood

00:00:18.878 --> 00:00:19.644
And the proof

00:00:19.456 --> 00:00:19.915
is in the

00:00:19.727 --> 00:00:20.257
pudding

00:00:20.411 --> 00:00:21.413
a new engine

00:00:21.225 --> 00:00:22.781
called unkernel runs

00:00:22.593 --> 00:00:23.512
two times to

00:00:23.324 --> 00:00:24.903
thirty-two times faster

00:00:24.715 --> 00:00:25.965
than qemu-wasm

00:00:26.071 --> 00:00:26.837
depending on the

00:00:26.649 --> 00:00:27.321
workload

00:00:27.380 --> 00:00:28.771
with benchmarks tracked

00:00:28.583 --> 00:00:29.396
over time

00:00:29.934 --> 00:00:30.948
Full story on

00:00:30.759 --> 00:00:31.655
the dashboard
